 1. format(3.14159, '.2f')                     -> '3.14'                     fixed decimals; f'{3.14159:.2f}' and '%.2f' % 3.14159 are the other spellings
 2. f'{3.14159:08.3f}'                         -> '0003.142'                 width 8, zero-filled, 3 decimals
 3. f'{123456.789:e}'                          -> '1.234568e+05'             scientific; f'{0.000123456:.3e}' is '1.235e-04', g picks a form: '1.23457e+06'
 4. f'{255:x} {255:b} {255:o}'                 -> 'ff 11111111 377'          bases without a prefix; #x #b #o give '0xff 0b11111111 0o377'
 5. f'{5:+d}|{42:05d}|{42:<5d}|'               -> '+5|00042|42   |'          a sign, zero fill, left alignment
 6. f'{-5:08b}'                                -> '-0000101'                 a negative keeps its minus sign, no two's complement; f'{-255:x}' is '-ff'
 7. format(2.675, '.2f')                       -> '2.67'                     the exact binary value is rounded: 2.665 gives 2.67 and 2.685 gives 2.69
 8. f'{1234567:,}'                             -> '1,234,567'                a thousands flag is built in; f'{1234567:_}' is '1_234_567', f'{1234567.891:,.2f}' is '1,234,567.89'
 9. hex(255), bin(255), format(255, 'x')       -> '0xff', '0b11111111', 'ff' hex/bin/oct carry a prefix; no to_s(36), but int('73', 36) reads it: 255
10. int('ff', 16), int('0x1f', 16), int('0x1f', 0) -> 255, 31, 31                back from a base; base 0 reads the prefix; int('zz', 16) is ValueError: int() always raises on junk
11. int('0b101', 0), int('1_000'), int('017', 8) -> 5, 1000, 15                a prefix needs base 0 or the matching base; underscores are fine
12. int('08')                                  -> 8                          a leading 0 is just a digit in base 10; int('017', 0) is ValueError
13. str(0.1 + 0.2), str(1e20)                  -> '0.30000000000000004', '1e+20' str is the shortest string that reads back as the same float; no .0 in the exponent form
14. str(999999999999999.9), str(1e15)          -> '999999999999999.9', '1000000000000000.0' positional up to 16 integer digits; exponent form from 17: str(1e16) is '1e+16'; small: str(1e-5) is '1e-05'
15. round(1234.5678, 2), round(1234.5678, -2)  -> 1234.57, 1200.0            round(x, -2) on a float stays a float; round(1250, -2) is 1200, half to even
16. str(round(3.1, 2)), f'{3.1:.2f}'           -> '3.1', '3.10'              round drops trailing zeros, format keeps them: money wants format, or Decimal
